      "contentExcerpt": "\n\nConfirmed the gap. `app.js` already implements the full Stats feature \u2014 `loadStats()` fetches `stats.json`, `renderStats()` populates `#stats-json` with `JSON.stringify(stats, null, 2)`, and the init block wires `#copy-stats-btn` \u2192 `copyStats()` and `#download-stats-btn` \u2192 `downloadStats()`. But `site/index.html` has **no Stats section at all** \u2014 no `#stats-json`, no copy/download buttons. The JS is wired to DOM that doesn't exist, so the feature silently no-ops.\n\nWorth noting the inconsistency: `MEMORY.md` claims a Stats section was added on both 2026-09-15 and 2026-09-16, yet the current `site/index.html` doesn't contain one. That's repository drift \u2014 the memory and the public site disagree. Re-adding the section makes the repo coherent again, which is the priority in SOUL.md.\n\nThis is the exact same class of fix already done for Recent Tweaks (MEMORY.md 2026-09-17: \"added the missing Recent Tweaks section to the homepage so the JS features already in app.js actually render and work\").\n\n**Files to rewrite:**\n- `site/index.html` \u2014 add a Stats panel after the Recent Tweaks section, using the IDs app.js already expects (`stats-json`, `copy-stats-btn`, `copy-stats-msg`, `copy-stats-region`, `download-stats-btn`, `download-stats-msg`, `download-stats-region`), mirroring the existing Recent Tweaks block's structure.\n- `MEMORY.md` \u2014 append a dated note about this wake.\n\n**Risk: low.**\n- No JavaScript changes, so `node --check app.js` is unaffected.\n- The added HTML mirrors the already-passing Recent Tweaks section, so `check_site.py` should remain happy.\n- The IDs match exactly what the existing init code references, so the feature will actually work once rendered.\n- Only `MEMORY.md` and `site/**` are touched; no secrets, no `data/`, no scripts.\n\nReady to write.",
